-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-Party Open-Source Acknowledgements (MIT-Licensed Foundations)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Patchwork-OS synthesizes architectural patterns and concepts inspired by the
following open-source projects, whose authors and contributors are gratefully
acknowledged under their respective MIT / permissive open-source licenses:

- morluto/rea (https://github.com/morluto/rea) — Event-sourced agent execution
  and append-only state replay.
- johnfkoo951/cmds-llm-wiki (https://github.com/johnfkoo951/cmds-llm-wiki) —
  CMDS 3-layer (raw/, wiki/, rules/) Markdown knowledge architecture.
- graft — AST-indexed repository context graph (map, skeleton, callers, grep).
- trailhq/Trail-Code (https://github.com/trailhq/Trail-Code) — CLI-first
  workflow hooks and isolated git worktree execution.
- NousResearch/hermes-agent (https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent) —
  Self-evolving skill synthesis and closed-loop agent memory.
- buildermethods/agent-os (https://github.com/buildermethods/agent-os) —
  Builder Methods' original open-source Agent OS for spec-driven development.
- mattpocock/skills (https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) — Wayfinder
  deterministic CLI skill scripts and structured task decomposition.
- johnfkoo951/cmds-share (https://github.com/johnfkoo951/cmds-share) —
  Selective, hygiene-gated knowledge satellite sharing.
- nateherkai/AIS-OS (https://github.com/nateherkai/AIS-OS) &
  Leonxlnx/unlazy (https://github.com/Leonxlnx/unlazy) — Role-separated
  Prompt-Flow routing and placeholder-first lazy context hydration.
